ean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-upper-reset-band"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-upper-reset-band"],"id":"long.thm-upper-reset-band","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.10 (Upper-reset dyadic-band escape, checked for $`13\\le d\\le30`$)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.10, p. 47, label thm:upper-reset-band","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*The upper-reset dyadic-band escape condition requires the following at every actual upper reset $d\\ge13$: for every $0\\le j\\le d$, the reset charge avoids a linear-width band immediately below the dyadic power $2^{d-j+1}$ ($2^{d-j+1}<\\mathrm{resetCharge}$ or $\\mathrm{resetCharge}+2(d+j)\\le 2^{d-j+1}$). Granted this, $1/2\\in\n\\ensuremath{\\mathcal A}$. The linked proof verifies this condition for $13\\le d\\le30$, using exact successor remainders at rows $14$–$31$ (for example, $\\mathrm{rem}(14)=392$ and $\\mathrm{rem}(31)=4187487147$). This finite verification does not supply the hypothesis for every $d\\ge13$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-upper-reset-band","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-upper-reset-band","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-upper-reset-band%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_of_upperResetDyadicBandEscape%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-upper-reset-band%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_of_upperResetDyadicBandEscape%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.half_m